From: pattex67 <33281022+pattex67@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:09:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] SPIR-V: global 32-bit atomics through storage buffers;
 task/mesh push constants

- Atomics on untracked global memory (add, min, max, and, or, xor, exchange) go
  through a helper that finds the storage buffer holding the address, like
  global loads and stores. Three Ocarina of Time forest computes failed to build
  without them. After zortos293/Lichii #87, which routes add and max.
- Task and mesh stages are in the push constant range and pushes of a mesh
  pipeline (after Djihads80/Eglantine #472, via Lichii #62).
- EDEN_NX2_MESH_FIRST=1 adds the draw's first vertex to the first stage's
  workgroup index (after zortos293/Lichii d7663205ba). Off by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
